# PROJECT STARTUP INSTRUCTIONS
## Bill's AI Glucose Management Bot ("Gemini")
### Everything you need to rebuild from scratch

---

## WHAT THIS PROJECT IS

A personal AI-powered diabetes management assistant that runs as a Telegram chatbot. Bill texts it naturally ("just ate pasta, about 60g carbs, glucose is 145"), and it calculates insulin doses using a pharmacokinetic model tuned to his specific biology, logs everything to GitHub, and pulls live CGM data from Nightscout. The AI (Claude) is stateless — all memory is externalized into files on GitHub and fetched fresh on every message.

**The bot is named "Gemini" in conversation but runs on Claude claude-sonnet-4-6.**

---

## THE FIVE FILES THAT DEFINE THE SYSTEM

Every parameter, every rule, every piece of logged history lives in these five files in the GitHub repo `williamjwells/pancreas`. There is no database, no server-side state.

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `Gemini_Model_Parameters.json` | All numeric dosing parameters (GSF, ICR, targets, IOB decay, etc.) |
| `Gemini_Behavior_Rules.txt` | Claude's complete instruction set — how to calculate, format, respond |
| `Gemini_Health_Log.jsonl` | Append-only log of every meal, insulin dose, and note |
| `glucose_telegram_bot.py` | The Python bot that wires everything together |
| `timeseries.jsonl` | CGM time series (historical reference, not used at runtime) |

Additionally:
- `Procfile` — tells Railway how to start the bot: `worker: python glucose_telegram_bot.py`
- `railway.toml` — watchPatterns so Railway auto-redeploys when config files change

