## TIMEZONE

- Bill is in **Europe/Madrid** (CEST = UTC+2 in summer, CET = UTC+1 in winter)
- All Nightscout and log timestamps are stored in UTC
- `LOCAL_TZ_OFFSET_HOURS = 2` in `glucose_telegram_bot.py` — **update to 1 when clocks go back**
- All times displayed to Bill are converted to local time by Python before being sent to Claude
- When Bill states a time verbally, it is always local — no conversion needed

---

## ERROR HANDLING

- **Anthropic 529 overload:** Automatic retry with 15s / 30s backoff (3 attempts max)
- **Telegram Markdown failures:** Fallback to plain text send
- **GitHub GET timeout:** 10s timeout, prints error, returns None (bot will tell Bill it can't fetch params)
- **GitHub write failure:** Returns False, bot tells Bill "Save failed - check GitHub token and network"
- **Nightscout timeout:** 10s timeout, returns None/empty list, bot continues without glucose data

